WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.100
Noor runs a fictional design studio.

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:08.140
She asks an AI to turn a supplier
quote into a neat form: supplier, item,

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.270
quantity and delivery date.

4
00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.450
The form comes back perfect.

5
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.290
Every field is filled, and every
value has the right format.

6
00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.179
But the delivery date
isn’t in the quote at all.

7
00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.718
That’s the difference
between shape and truth.

8
00:00:21.858 --> 00:00:25.448
Some AI services offer structured outputs.

9
00:00:25.448 --> 00:00:29.095
OpenAI’s documentation
says the feature ensures

10
00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.920
responses adhere to the schema you supply.

11
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.120
A schema is the shape:
which fields exist,

12
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.550
and what kind of value
each one holds.

13
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.300
The same documentation says

14
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.267
structured outputs can
still contain mistakes.

15
00:00:42.407 --> 00:00:45.417
In Noor’s atelier, every
card fits its slot.

16
00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:47.917
But each slot also has a source lamp.

17
00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:51.757
The delivery date fits perfectly,
and its lamp stays red.

18
00:00:51.897 --> 00:00:53.897
So run three separate checks.

19
00:00:53.897 --> 00:00:55.800
First, is the format valid?

20
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.387
Second, does each value match the source?

21
00:00:58.387 --> 00:01:00.694
Third, does it follow your business rules?

22
00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:05.534
If the information isn’t there, the
right answer is unknown, not a guess.

23
00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:09.094
Leave room in the form for
unknown, and send it to a person.

24
00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:13.674
Also plan for the times an
AI declines, or stops early.

25
00:01:13.674 --> 00:01:16.904
The documentation says
refusals can be detected.

26
00:01:16.904 --> 00:01:19.197
Your system still has to handle them.

27
00:01:19.337 --> 00:01:22.317
And features differ between
models and services,

28
00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:25.210
so check what your own
setup actually supports.

29
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:30.225
Noor checks the date against the quote,
marks it unknown, and asks the supplier.

30
00:01:30.365 --> 00:01:32.455
A tidy form is easier to check.

31
00:01:32.455 --> 00:01:33.575
It isn’t proof.

32
00:01:33.575 --> 00:01:36.195
Check the shape, the
source, and the rules.

33
00:01:36.335 --> 00:01:37.805
Ahmadreza Samadi.

34
00:01:37.805 --> 00:01:39.742
